 "short": "Entropy changes along reversible paths",
 "lead": "An expansion into a vacuum takes in no heat, yet the gas ends in the same state as a reversible expansion does, so the entropy change is found along the reversible path. The same reasoning applied to two gases that mix gives the entropy of mixing.",
